1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:02,700
Ear.

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:05,480
Consciousness.

3
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:21,400
One of the most important things that one needs to understand about a person is that a person is asleep.

4
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:30,040
He does not wake up even when he thinks that he has woken up.

5
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,980
His awakening is very fragile.

6
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:43,240
His awakening is so tiny that it should not be taken into account at all.

7
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:50,700
His wisdom is not only beautiful, but a completely empty name.

8
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:55,300
You sleep at night.

9
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,160
You sleep during the day.

10
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:06,580
From birth to death you continue to move from one image from one dream to another.

11
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:11,680
But you never really wake up.

12
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:18,580
Don't fool yourself by waking up just by opening your eyes.

13
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,880
Until you open your eyes again.

14
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,340
Until you learn to see.

15
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:36,080
Do you see who you are?

16
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:41,580
Don't think that you are growing up.

17
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:47,000
This is the greatest visibility that a person lives in.

18
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:58,800
If you assume that you have woken up, it cannot be that you are making an effort to really wake up.

19
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:01,640
www.mooji.org

